  "tutLessonTipsTitle": "Winning tips",
  "tutValuesIntro": "ShadowHand is a memory game for two. Each player has cards face down. When the game ends, everyone adds up their cards — the lowest total wins.",
  "tutValuesChart": "Each card is worth points. Ace = 1, number cards = their number, Jack = 11, Queen = 12, red King = 13. The best cards: a black King is worth 0 and a Joker is worth −1!",
  "tutValuesQuizLowest": "Quick quiz: tap the card worth the fewest points.",
  "tutValuesQuizLowestWrong": "Not quite. The Joker is worth −1 — even lower than an Ace.",
  "tutValuesQuizKing": "Two Kings here. Tap the one worth 0 points.",
  "tutValuesQuizKingWrong": "Only black Kings (♠ ♣) are worth 0. Red Kings (♥ ♦) are worth 13 — the worst card in the deck!",
  "tutValuesDone": "Perfect! Your goal: keep low cards and get rid of high ones.",
  "tutDealIntro": "Each player gets 4 cards face down in a row. You don't know what they are yet — and neither does your opponent.",
  "tutDealReveal": "Before play starts, you get one quick look. Tap Reveal.",
  "tutDealMemorize": "Your two cards on the left are shown for a few seconds. Remember them: a 2 and an 8!",
  "tutDealQuiz": "They're face down again. Where is your 2? Tap it.",
  "tutDealQuizWrong": "The 2 was your first card, on the far left. Memory is everything in this game!",
  "tutDealDone": "Right! Your other two cards are still a mystery — you'll learn more as you play.",
  "tutDrawPrompt": "It's your turn. Tap the deck to draw a card.",
  "tutSwapIntro": "You remember your first two cards: a 2 and a 9. A 9 costs a lot of points — let's replace it.",
  "tutSwapPick": "You drew a 3. That's better than your 9! Tap your 9 (second card) to swap them.",
  "tutSwapPickWrong": "Tap your 9 — the second card from the left. Swapping a card you don't know is a gamble.",
  "tutSwapDone": "The 3 goes face down where the 9 was, and the 9 goes to the discard pile. That ends your turn — and you just saved 6 points.",
  "tutThrowPick": "Ouch — a red King, worth 13. You don't want it! Tap the drawn card to throw it on the discard pile.",
  "tutThrowWrong": "Don't keep a bad card. Tap the drawn card (bottom left) to throw it away.",
  "tutThrowDone": "Thrown away! Your cards didn't change and your turn is over. Throw any card that wouldn't make your hand better.",
  "tutDoubleIntro": "You remember your first card is a 5.",
  "tutDoublePick": "Another 5! When the card you draw has the same rank as one of yours, tap your card: both get discarded.",
  "tutDoubleWrong": "Tap your 5 — the first card on the left.",
  "tutDoubleDone": "Both 5s are gone and you have one card fewer. Fewer cards means fewer points — and if you run out of cards, the game ends.",
  "tutMatchIntro": "You remember your first card is a 7. Now it's your opponent's turn…",
  "tutMatchPick": "Your opponent threw a 7! On your turn, before you draw, you can tap a card with the same rank as the top of the discard pile to get rid of it. Tap your 7.",
  "tutMatchWrong": "Tap your 7 — the first card on the left.",
  "tutMatchContinue": "A free discard! Matching doesn't end your turn: you can match again, and then you still draw. Tap the deck.",
  "tutMatchThrow": "An 8 — not great. Tap it to throw it and end your turn.",
  "tutMatchGuess": "Next turn, the top card is a 4. You think your middle card might be a 4… but you're not sure. Let's see what a wrong guess does: tap it.",
  "tutMatchPenalty": "Wrong — it wasn't a 4. You get a penalty card from the deck, face down, and the card you tapped stays. Only match when you're sure!",
  "tutJackPeekButton": "A Jack! When you draw a Jack you can peek at any one card — yours or your opponent's. Tap Peek.",
  "tutJackPick": "Now tap the card you want to see. Let's spy on your opponent's second card.",
  "tutJackPickWrong": "Tap your opponent's second card from the left.",
  "tutJackReveal": "It's a Queen — 12 points for them. Remember where it is: it hides again in a moment.",
  "tutJackDone": "After the peek, the Jack is thrown automatically and your turn ends. The power is optional: you can also keep or throw a Jack like any other card.",
  "tutQueenIntro": "You remember your second card is a 10. Let's give it to your opponent.",
  "tutQueenButtons": "A Queen! You get a choice. Shuffle mixes up one player's cards. Replace swaps one of your cards with one of theirs. Tap Replace.",
  "tutQueenButtonsWrong": "For this lesson, tap Replace.",
  "tutQueenPickYours": "First tap the card you want to give away: your 10, the second card.",
  "tutQueenPickYoursWrong": "Tap your 10 — your second card from the left.",
  "tutQueenPickTheirs": "Now tap the opponent's card you want to take: their first card.",
  "tutQueenPickTheirsWrong": "Tap your opponent's first card, on the left.",
  "tutQueenDone": "Swapped! Your 10 now belongs to your opponent. You don't see the card you got, but most cards are worth less than 10 — a good deal. The Queen is thrown after use.",
  "tutQueenShuffle": "Shuffle is the other option: mix up your opponent's cards and everything they remembered becomes useless. You can also shuffle your own cards.",
  "tutEndIntro": "The game ends in one of two ways: a player has no cards left, or someone taps End game.",
  "tutEndPress": "Think your total is lower? Either player can tap End game at any time. Try it.",
  "tutEndCount": "All cards are revealed. Add up yours: 3 + 2 + black King + Joker. What's your total?",
  "tutEndCountWrong": "Remember: a black King is 0 and a Joker is −1. So 3 + 2 + 0 − 1 = 4.",
  "tutEndWinner": "Your opponent has 9 + 5 + 7 + 1 = 22. Who wins?",
  "tutEndWinnerWrong": "The lowest total wins: 4 beats 22.",
  "tutEndDone": "You win! If both totals are equal, it's a tie.",
  "tutTipMemory": "Tip 1 — Remember everything. Every card you see — at the start, when you swap, with a Jack — tells you something. Keep track of it.",
  "tutTipKeepLow": "Tip 2 — Keep black Kings and Jokers. They're worth 0 and −1: never swap them away.",
  "tutTipDiscard": "Tip 3 — Watch the discard pile. Every card your opponent throws is a chance to match one of yours for free.",
  "tutTipQueen": "Tip 4 — Use Queens well. Give away your highest card, or Shuffle to wreck your opponent's memory.",
